Chapter: ProbeTryingFail
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 `fail` does not fail here, and `trying` does not try.

 `fail` was the last builtin with 70 call sites and no assertion anywhere.
 Reading it turned up something better than a missing test: on bare metal it
 does not terminate at all. `emit-fail-builtin` (Emit/X86_64Builtins.codex:908)
 evaluates the message, DISCARDS it, stores 1 at `try-fail-flag-addr`, and
 returns 0. Execution continues.

 It is a signal, not a panic, and the thing that reads the signal is Codex's
 retry construct:

     trying N times
       ...body...
     falling back to
       ...fallback...
     end

 `emit-try-check-flag` (Emit/X86_64.codex:1487) reloads that flag after each
 statement of the body and branches when it is set, so a failed attempt is
 retried up to N times and then the fallback runs.

 THE PLUG IMPLEMENTS NEITHER HALF.

     fail    -> @panic(<message>), which terminates
     IrTry   -> `emit-zig-act body ctx d (zig-type-is-void ty)`

 That second one is the worse of the two. It emits the BODY and silently
 discards `fb` and `fail-stmts` -- the fallback and the failure handler are
 not refused, not marked, not mentioned; they are simply not there. It is the
 same shape as the `IrVecPat` defect this emitter already carries a warning
 about: an unhandled construct mapped onto a valid-but-different one, which
 produces a wrong program with no diagnostic.

 So a retry that bare metal recovers from kills this arm twice over: `fail`
 panics before the flag would be checked, and even if it did not, there is no
 fallback to reach.

 The success case is tested FIRST and deliberately. `trying` around a body
 that never fails works on both arms, because emitting just the body is
 accidentally right when nothing fails -- which is precisely why 70 `fail`
 sites and six `trying` blocks sit in the compiler with the ladder green.

Section: Main

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
   print-line-uni "-- a trying block whose body SUCCEEDS: both arms should agree --"
   trying 2 times
     print-line-uni "body ran once"
   falling back to
     print-line-uni "FELL BACK -- should not print in the success case"
   end
   print-line-uni "-- a trying block whose body FAILS: bare metal recovers --"
   trying 2 times
     print-line-uni "attempt"
     fail "deliberate failure"
   falling back to
     print-line-uni "fell back, and the program is still alive"
   end
   print-line-uni "-- reached the end, so this arm has a working retry --"
  end
